# Local simulation of the three-host topology — `make mh-up`.
#
# WHAT THIS SIMULATES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
# -----------------------------------------
# Three Compose projects, each with its OWN Docker network. There is no shared
# network and therefore no Compose DNS between them: a container on node B
# cannot resolve `kafka1`, exactly as it could not if node A were a different
# machine. Every cross-node connection has to go out through a published port
# and back in, over an address that resolves off-node.
#
# That is the property that breaks real multi-host deployments, and it is
# genuinely reproduced here. `make mh-drill` asserts the isolation before it
# asserts anything else, so this claim is checked rather than believed.
#
# It does NOT reproduce: network partitions, cross-datacentre latency, or a
# hardware failure. Killing every container in a project is a close analogue of
# losing a machine — the processes die at once and the data on that node's
# volumes stays put — but it is not the same thing.
#
# ADDRESSING
# ----------
# Docker Desktop containers cannot reach this Mac's LAN IP (verified: connect
# times out), so the routable address for all three "hosts" is
# host.docker.internal. Node identity is therefore carried entirely by the
# port. On real hosts the addresses differ and every port below goes back to
# its natural value — the SHAPE of the config is identical, which is the point.
NODE_A_HOST=host.docker.internal
NODE_B_HOST=host.docker.internal
NODE_C_HOST=host.docker.internal

# --- node A: kafka1, redis primary, sentinel 1, minio, jobmanager -----------
KAFKA_A_BROKER_PORT=19092
KAFKA_A_CTRL_PORT=19093
KAFKA_A_HOST_PORT=19094
REDIS_A_PORT=16379
SENTINEL_A_PORT=16380
MINIO_PORT=19000
MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT=19001
# The JobManager publishes 1:1 — only one node runs one, and blob.server.port
# has no bind-port setting, so published must equal bound.
JM_REST_PORT=8081
JM_RPC_PORT=6123
JM_BLOB_PORT=6124
JM_METRICS_PORT=9250
PROM_PORT=9090

# --- node B: kafka2, redis replica, sentinel 2, taskmanager -----------------
KAFKA_B_BROKER_PORT=19192
KAFKA_B_CTRL_PORT=19193
KAFKA_B_HOST_PORT=19194
REDIS_B_PORT=16479
SENTINEL_B_PORT=16480
TM_B_RPC_PORT=16122
TM_B_DATA_PORT=16121
TM_B_METRICS_PORT=19251

# --- node C: kafka3, sentinel 3, taskmanager --------------------------------
KAFKA_C_BROKER_PORT=19292
KAFKA_C_CTRL_PORT=19293
KAFKA_C_HOST_PORT=19294
SENTINEL_C_PORT=16580
TM_C_RPC_PORT=16222
TM_C_DATA_PORT=16221
TM_C_METRICS_PORT=19252

# --- credentials (dev defaults; a real deployment injects these) ------------
CLUSTER_ID=petafs-mh-cluster-1
KAFKA_USER=petafs
KAFKA_PASSWORD=petafs-dev-secret
REDIS_PASSWORD=petafs-dev-secret
TLS_STOREPASS=petafs-dev-secret
MINIO_USER=petafs
MINIO_PASSWORD=petafs-dev-secret
